    {
      "id": "967oCrEteMDRzCaeKyhbn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -19806.225192839047,
      "y": -4591.949164055999,
      "width": 636.29931640625,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 176219706,
      "version": 1196,
      "versionNonce": 1975431846,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794651781475,
      "created": 1794642440224,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "There are many ways of cloning repo\n\n1.https\ngit clone  https://github.com/shashikanth16193/swe-daily-learnings.git\n\n2.ssh\ngit clone  https://github.com/shashikanth16193/swe-daily-learnings.git\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "There are many ways of cloning repo\n\n1.https\ngit clone  https://github.com/shashikanth16193/swe-daily-learnings.git\n\n2.ssh\ngit clone  https://github.com/shashikanth16193/swe-daily-learnings.git\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "m0SzpyOrMCXNNG3LqL1Pg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -21213.566750088357,
      "y": -4568.986468684938,
      "width": 1134.4795792225123,
      "height": 2900,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6M",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1018147066,
      "version": 5258,
      "versionNonce": 2111663590,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794651781475,
      "created": 1794642624884,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "creating repository in local and push\n\ncd ~\ncd Documents/my-project\n\ngit init \nso it basically creates .git folder in our /my-project folder\n\nbut above way is naive\n\n\n\ncreating repository in github \n\ngit clone repository \nclones empty branches at all both in local and remote\n\ncreate a devlop branch in the remote and make it default branch\n\n\n\norign \nit is vairable that stores git hub repo url and presnt in .git/config folder\n\nso when we try to push or fetch from the remote using git fetch origin or git push origin\nthen git sees nearest .git folder and checks url inside origin variable and from there it goes to corresponding remote\nbut if we have multi repo then git will try to push changes in wrong origin \n\nso explictly set origin\ngit remote set-url <my-project-url>\n\n\n\ngit fetch origin \nfetches new changes from remote\nwhy? if we try to create branch before fetching changes from remote we will be on lag\nso in our case we didnt fetched devlop branch at all from remote meaning if we create branch directly without fetching it we\ndont have devlop changes at all meaning our branch is behind devlop\nfetch means download all metad data and commits from remote to .git folder \n\ngit pull origin  ==> git fetch + git merge\nfetches the changes and merges the changes that were not there into our current branch\ndanger -cause it causes merge conflicts\n\n\ndevlop\nconfigured as default branch in our remote \n\ngit branch\ndisplays all branches \ninitially there would be devlop branche\n\ngit checkout devlop\nswitchs from master to devlop\n\ngit checkout -b feature/sb-PAYFAC-16193-daily \ncreates branch from the devlop and checks out to our feature branch\nwe get all devlop changes from remote\n\n\ngit checkout -b feature/junior-PAYFAC-16193-daily \ncreates branch from current branch so new branch gets current branch changes\njuniour wants to work on same ticket as you which you already made changes so juniour creates branch from your branch\nso he get changes from your branch\n\n\ngit add . \nwe make changes to our files or add new files in our branch\nthey wont be tarcked by git unless we add them to .git folder which is called as staging area \n \ngit status\nto check which were modified and all \n\ngit commit -m \"learnings: zsh shell ,packagemanager\"\nit commits the files in staging area into the branch\n\ngit fetch origin \nfetches all new changes from devlop into our current branch\nso our branch will be up to date or else it will be lagged again \n\ngit push -u origin feature/sb-PAYFAC-16193-daily \npublishes our branch to remote url mentioned in the origin vairable\nfrom next commit on wards we can directly push without branch name\n\n\nHEAD it is like pointer refers  but always points to current branch\n\ngit push -u origin HEAD \npushes the current branch into origin\n\ngit reset --soft HEAD~1\nreverts the last commmit in current branch in local repository but changes are staged\n\ngit reset --soft HEAD~2\nreverts the last but one commit in current branch in local repository\n\n\ngit reset --hard HEAD~1\nsame as git reset soft but changes are completely removed in local too\n\n\n\ngit fetch origin  \nit fetches all branches\n\ngit fetch origin devlop\nit fetches devlop branch\n\ngit fetch origin feature/sb-0000-daily\nit fetches feature branch only\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "creating repository in local and push\n\ncd ~\ncd Documents/my-project\n\ngit init \nso it basically creates .git folder in our /my-project folder\n\nbut above way is naive\n\n\n\ncreating repository in github \n\ngit clone repository \nclones empty branches at all both in local and remote\n\ncreate a devlop branch in the remote and make it default branch\n\n\n\norign \nit is vairable that stores git hub repo url and presnt in .git/config folder\n\nso when we try to push or fetch from the remote using git fetch origin or git push origin\nthen git sees nearest .git folder and checks url inside origin variable and from there it goes to corresponding remote\nbut if we have multi repo then git will try to push changes in wrong origin \n\nso explictly set origin\ngit remote set-url <my-project-url>\n\n\n\ngit fetch origin \nfetches new changes from remote\nwhy? if we try to create branch before fetching changes from remote we will be on lag\nso in our case we didnt fetched devlop branch at all from remote meaning if we create branch directly without fetching it we dont have devlop changes at all meaning our branch is behind devlop\nfetch means download all metad data and commits from remote to .git folder \n\ngit pull origin  ==> git fetch + git merge\nfetches the changes and merges the changes that were not there into our current branch\ndanger -cause it causes merge conflicts\n\n\ndevlop\nconfigured as default branch in our remote \n\ngit branch\ndisplays all branches \ninitially there would be devlop branche\n\ngit checkout devlop\nswitchs from master to devlop\n\ngit checkout -b feature/sb-PAYFAC-16193-daily \ncreates branch from the devlop and checks out to our feature branch\nwe get all devlop changes from remote\n\n\ngit checkout -b feature/junior-PAYFAC-16193-daily \ncreates branch from current branch so new branch gets current branch changes\njuniour wants to work on same ticket as you which you already made changes so juniour creates branch from your branch\nso he get changes from your branch\n\n\ngit add . \nwe make changes to our files or add new files in our branch\nthey wont be tarcked by git unless we add them to .git folder which is called as staging area \n \ngit status\nto check which were modified and all \n\ngit commit -m \"learnings: zsh shell ,packagemanager\"\nit commits the files in staging area into the branch\n\ngit fetch origin \nfetches all new changes from devlop into our current branch\nso our branch will be up to date or else it will be lagged again \n\ngit push -u origin feature/sb-PAYFAC-16193-daily \npublishes our branch to remote url mentioned in the origin vairable\nfrom next commit on wards we can directly push without branch name\n\n\nHEAD it is like pointer refers  but always points to current branch\n\ngit push -u origin HEAD \npushes the current branch into origin\n\ngit reset --soft HEAD~1\nreverts the last commmit in current branch in local repository but changes are staged\n\ngit reset --soft HEAD~2\nreverts the last but one commit in current branch in local repository\n\n\ngit reset --hard HEAD~1\nsame as git reset soft but changes are completely removed in local too\n\n\n\ngit fetch origin  \nit fetches all branches\n\ngit fetch origin devlop\nit fetches devlop branch\n\ngit fetch origin feature/sb-0000-daily\nit fetches feature branch only\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
