      "updated": 1794652519435,
      "created": 1794651869900,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "~\nalways represesnts the home folder we can start from home folder when we got any\nconfusion \n\nls\nlist the files in current folder\n\nls -a\nlist all +hidden files\n\nls -la\nlist all +hidden files and also its permissions\n\ncd ~ + ls \nmost helpful command\n\ncd ..\nto go back one level\n\ncd - \nto go back on folder \n\n\npwd\nshows full path of current working directory\n\nrm <file>\nremove file\n\nrf <folder>\nremove folder\n\nmv <source> <dest> (Move / Rename)\nmove or rename file\n\ncp <source> <dest> (Copy): \nCopies a file\n\ncp -r <folder1> <folder2> to copy an entire folder\n\ncat <file> (Concatenate)\nReads and prints the entire content of a file directly in your terminal\n\ntouch <file>\nCreates a brand-new empty file instantly \n\nsed\nFinds and replaces text inside a file without opening an editor",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "~\nalways represesnts the home folder we can start from home folder when we got any confusion \n\nls\nlist the files in current folder\n\nls -a\nlist all +hidden files\n\nls -la\nlist all +hidden files and also its permissions\n\ncd ~ + ls \nmost helpful command\n\ncd ..\nto go back one level\n\ncd - \nto go back on folder \n\n\npwd\nshows full path of current working directory\n\nrm <file>\nremove file\n\nrf <folder>\nremove folder\n\nmv <source> <dest> (Move / Rename)\nmove or rename file\n\ncp <source> <dest> (Copy): \nCopies a file\n\ncp -r <folder1> <folder2> to copy an entire folder\n\ncat <file> (Concatenate)\nReads and prints the entire content of a file directly in your terminal\n\ntouch <file>\nCreates a brand-new empty file instantly \n\nsed\nFinds and replaces text inside a file without opening an editor",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
